Morelia Change.log
==================

2026-10-29
---------------------------------------------------------

Desmond MM-PBSA moved to a standalone application
  * Removed the bundled bin/desmond_gmxMMPBSA/ subfolder; the Desmond-to-
    gmx_MMPBSA workflow is now developed and installed as a standalone
    application outside Morelia (default location $HOME/desmond_gmxMMPBSA/).
  * morelia.py: the Gromacs menu item "Desmond MM-PBSA" now launches the
    external command pref.cmdDesmond_gmxMMPBSA through the shell instead
    of running the bundled GUI script.
  * preferences.py: new cmdDesmond_gmxMMPBSA setting pointing to the local
    installation of the standalone application; install, doc, example and
    external-application directories switched to $HOME-based paths.



2026-10-15
---------------------------------------------------------

morelia.py
  * New YASARA menu items:
      - Docking - create complexes -> docking_complexes.py
      - Top poses energies         -> top_pose_E.py
      - YOb from smi               -> smi_em_yob.py

New scripts (bin/)
  * docking_complexes.py - creates YASARA docking complex scenes: for each
                           ligand .yob in the working directory it adds the
                           ligand to the *_complex.sce (receptor + docking
                           box) and saves receptor-base_ligand_complex.sce
                           into a receptor-base_ligand subfolder.
  * top_pose_E.py        - extracts energies of top docking poses into
                           top_poses_E.csv.
  * smi_em_yob.py        - converts smi ligands to energy-minimized YOb
                           files (via YASARA/smi_em_yob.mcr).

New YASARA macros (bin/YASARA/)
  * docking_complex.mcr  - macro template used by docking_complexes.py.
  * smi_em_yob.mcr       - macro template used by smi_em_yob.py.



2026-10-02
---------------------------------------------------------

morelia.py
  * New YASARA menu item:
      - Ligand distance    -> yasara_distance_app.py

sort_poses.py
  * If <target>_distances.tab (produced by yasara_distance_app.py) exists,
    the per-pose receptor-ligand distances are appended as the last column
    of <target>_sorted.csv.

New scripts (bin/)
  * yasara_distance_app.py - wx GUI that writes and runs a YASARA macro
                             measuring the distance between a receptor
                             residue atom and a ligand atom (name or
                             element) for every docking pose; saves
                             <target>_distances.tab.



2026-09-08
---------------------------------------------------------

morelia.py
  * New "AutoDock" menu with items:
      - smi to pdbqt       -> smi2pdbqt.py
      - pdb to pdbqt       -> pdb2pdbqt.py
      - Map receptor       -> map_receptor.py
      - Batch docking      -> batch_dock.py
  * New YASARA menu items:
      - Dock - Extract top poses   -> extract_top_poses.py
      - Make Si ligands topologies -> make_usertopo.py
      - Minimize Si ligands        -> minimize_si_ligands.py

pdb_pymol.py
  * File dialog filter relaxed from *.pdb to *.pdb* (also matches .pdbqt).

New scripts (bin/)
  * smi2pdbqt.py         - batch SMILES -> PDBQT converter (RDKit + Meeko), wx GUI.
  * pdb2pdbqt.py         - receptor PDB -> PDBQT converter (Meeko), wx GUI.
  * map_receptor.py      - AutoGrid receptor mapping front-end, wx GUI.
  * batch_dock.py        - batch docking with AutoDock-GPU, wx GUI.
  * extract_top_poses.py - extract top-ranked poses from docking archives.
  * make_usertopo.py     - generate YASARA usertopo_<NAME>.fof residue
                           topology for silicon-containing ligands
                           (C-analog GAFF2/AM1BCC parameterization, Si swapped
                           back with formal charge).
  * minimize_si_ligands.py - batch pipeline: detect Si in .sdf files, generate
                           usertopo templates via make_usertopo.py, rebuild
                           force fields, run YASARA minimization.



2026-08-04  commit 0284f5d "Bug fixes"
---------------------------------------

Desmond analysis scripts (bin/)
  * Lig_RMSD.py, PL_Contacts.py, Prot_BB_RMSD.py, Prot_RMSF.py rewritten:
    modular functions instead of exec()-based hacks, support for one or more
    input directories, matplotlib plotting, and proper wx error dialogs.

Desmond -> gmx_MMPBSA workflow (bin/desmond_gmxMMPBSA/)
  * Engine desmond_gmxmmpbsa.py bumped 7.1.0 -> 9.1.0:
      - support for the NMA methylamide cap (mapped to ff19SB NME),
      - explicit cap atom-name alias resolution (CH3/CA, HH3x/xHH3/HAx/xHA)
        instead of relying on one historical naming convention,
      - template-prefix handling for N-/C-terminal residue variants,
      - geometric validation of mapped template bonds.
  * GUI desmond_gmxmmpbsa_wx.py bumped 1.0.3 -> 1.0.6; dependency check now
    also requires scipy.
  * New steric_preflight.py: topology-aware steric clash preflight for
    prepared trajectories using the Amber COM.prmtop Lennard-Jones
    parameters; only synthetic ACE/NME cap atoms are moved automatically.
  * New helper scripts run_capfixed_recovery.sh (re-run single-trajectory
    gmx_MMPBSA from validated *_capfix files) and run_gmx_structure_route.sh
    (build Amber topologies directly from prepared PDB + Antechamber MOL2,
    bypassing the ParmEd Amber -> GROMACS -> Amber round-trip).
  * Timestamped .backup_* copies of engine, GUI, cap-repair and force-field
    files archived under bin/desmond_gmxMMPBSA/.

